00:15:46.000 --> 00:16:30.000
Often what we'll see is that people will have some relief with SSRIs and then they will add the combined oral contraceptive. I do think it's important to note that other combined oral contraceptives that contain other progestins, so not drospirinone, but some of the other ones, those have not beat placebo in clinical trials, and they have been tested. So it does seem that there may be something special about this particular oral contraceptive or family of contraceptives that contain drospirinone. We're not 100% sure why they work better, but that is the next step. And so both of those are FDA-approved for the treatment of PMDD. Often we'll see people do SSRIs and then add an oral contraceptive or switch to an oral contraceptive. If those treatments have

